---
import PublicLayout from "../components/PublicLayout.astro";
const sections = [["Start with a device", "start"], ["Try it with your agent", "devices"], ["Connect the flow", "flow"], ["Choose an interface", "interfaces"], ["Build your own", "build"]];
const buildPrompt = "Read https://www.openlaunch.dev/docs/sdk.md and https://www.openlaunch.dev/docs/functions.md. Help me build an openlaunch adapter for my device, publish its actual functions, and test an action end to end. Use the live API schemas. Keep device setup credentials, device credentials and agent credentials separate. Have me enter credentials privately in my terminal, never in chat.";
---
<PublicLayout title="openlaunch · Your agents. Your devices." sections={sections}>
  <div class="workbench">
    <section class="intro">
      <h1>Your agents. Your devices.</h1>
      <p class="intro-copy">Hardware, Linux computers, and your Home Assistant home.<br class="desktop-break" /> Connected to the agents you already use.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="primary-link" href="/console/">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <button class="build-prompt" type="button" data-copy-prompt={buildPrompt}>
          <span class="agent-marks" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/logos/claude.svg" width="24" height="24" alt="" /><img src="/logos/codex.svg" width="24" height="24" alt="" /><img src="/logos/cursor.svg" width="24" height="24" alt="" /></span>
          <span data-copy-label aria-live="polite">Build with your agent</span>
          <span class="copy-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="copy-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="17" height="17" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="1.5" /><path d="M13 7V3H3v10h4" /></svg><svg class="check-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="17" height="17" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="m3 10 4 4 10-10" /></svg></span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <p class="intro-note">Keep it on your own machine? <a href="/docs/cli">CLI</a>, <a href="/docs/sdk">SDK</a>, or <a href="/docs/architecture#deployment">self-hosted <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></p>
      <p class="copy-fallback" hidden>Copy this prompt: <span>{buildPrompt}</span></p>
    </section>
    <section class="start-section" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <h2 id="start-title">Start with something useful.</h2>
      <p class="section-copy">Connect a computer, bring your home into the loop, or add a device of your own.</p>
      <div class="starter-grid">
        <a class="starter" href="/docs/linux"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="12" rx="2" /><path d="M8 20h8m-4-4v4m-5-9 2-2-2-2m4 4h5" /></svg><h3>A Linux computer</h3><p>Inspect your Pi, open a browser, and control its desktop with the access you enable.</p><span>Set up Linux <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
        <a class="starter" href="/docs/home-assistant"><svg class="ha-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m3 10 9-7 9 7M5 9v12h14V9M10 21v-7h4v7" /></svg><h3>Your Home Assistant home</h3><p>Discover entities, run scenes and scripts, and call your connected devices’ functions.</p><span>Connect Home Assistant <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
        <a class="starter" href="/docs/sdk"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="6" width="12" height="12" rx="2" /><path d="M9 2v4m6-4v4M9 18v4m6-4v4M2 9h4m-4 6h4m12-6h4m-4 6h4" /></svg><h3>A device you build</h3><p>Start with an Uno or ESP32, or write an adapter for the hardware you have.</p><span>Explore the SDK <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="example-section" id="devices" aria-labelledby="example-title">
      <h2 id="example-title">Ask for what you actually need.</h2>
      <p class="section-copy">Your agent reads the device’s functions, requests an action, and follows its receipt.</p>
      <div class="examples">
        <article><span class="example-label">01 / Linux</span><blockquote>“Find my Pi’s specs, then open YouTube on its desktop.”</blockquote><p>System information, browser launch, and a screenshot to see the result.</p><a href="/docs/linux">See Linux functions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
        <article><span class="example-label">02 / Home Assistant</span><blockquote>“Turn on the test toggle, read its state, then turn it off.”</blockquote><p>A real service call and state read. Start with a helper; no hardware needed.</p><a href="/docs/home-assistant#test-without-physical-devices">Try the test helper <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
        <article><span class="example-label">03 / Your hardware</span><blockquote>“Show ‘hello’ on my Uno, then check its health.”</blockquote><p>Built-in functions today. Add your own handlers as your project grows.</p><a href="/docs/uno-r4">Connect an Uno <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      </div>
      <p class="example-note">Example requests. Available functions depend on your adapter and saved grants. <a href="/docs/status">See what’s been verified →</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="flow-section" id="flow" aria-labelledby="flow-title">
      <h2 id="flow-title">Put your devices in the flow.</h2>
      <p class="section-copy">One device or a whole Home Assistant installation. Your agent uses the same connection.</p>
      <div class="flow-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Your agent connects to openlaunch, then to a device adapter or Home Assistant gateway, and on to your devices.">
        <span>Your agent<small>ChatGPT · Codex · Any MCP client</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span class="flow-hub">openlaunch<small>Functions · Access · Receipts</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Adapter or gateway<small>Linux · Home Assistant · SDK</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Your devices<small>Computers · Homes · Hardware</small></span>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-notes"><p><strong>Choose the access.</strong> Grant individual functions, choose an expiry, and revoke access from your console.</p><p><strong>Follow the result.</strong> See what was queued, delivered and reported. Device state and physical verification stay distinct.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="interface-section" id="interfaces" aria-labelledby="interface-title">
      <h2 id="interface-title">Use the interface that fits.</h2>
      <div class="interface-list">
        <a href="/docs/agents"><span>MCP</span><p>Connect ChatGPT, Codex or another agent. Discover functions as you need them.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>
        <a href="/docs/reference"><span>API</span><p>Build on the same device catalog, grants and action receipts over HTTPS.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>
        <a href="/docs/cli"><span>ol CLI</span><p>Install once. Inspect devices and invoke their functions from your terminal.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="build-section" id="build" aria-labelledby="build-title">
      <div><h2 id="build-title">Your hardware.<br />Your functions.</h2><p class="section-copy">Describe the inputs. Write the handler. Connect your agent.</p></div>
      <div><p>Adapters publish the functions they actually implement. Your agent discovers the current schema through MCP, API or CLI, with the same permission checks across all three.</p><div class="links"><a href="/docs/functions">Build a function →</a><a href="https://github.com/pkyanam/openlaunch">Read the source ↗</a></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="closing"><h2>Start with one device.</h2><p>Free hosted access. MIT licensed. Self-host it when you want.</p><a class="primary-link" href="/console/">Open your console <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/pricing">See pricing →</a><a href="/changelog">Latest updates →</a></section>
  </div>
</PublicLayout>
<script>
  document.addEventListener("click", async (event) => {
    const button = (event.target as Element)?.closest<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy-prompt]");
    if (!button || button.disabled) return;
    const label = button.querySelector("[data-copy-label]")!;
    button.disabled = true;
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copyPrompt!);
      button.dataset.copied = "true";
      label.textContent = "Prompt copied";
    } catch {
      label.textContent = "Select the prompt below";
      document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".copy-fallback")!.hidden = false;
    }
    window.setTimeout(() => { label.textContent = "Build with your agent"; delete button.dataset.copied; button.disabled = false; }, 2500);
  });
</script>
<style>
  .workbench { --ink: var(--blume-foreground, #171717); --muted: var(--blume-muted-foreground, #666); --line: var(--blume-border, #dedede); --paper: var(--blume-background, #fff); max-width: 1220px; margin: auto; padding: 72px clamp(32px, 5vw, 88px) 64px; color: var(--ink); }
  .workbench * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  .workbench a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .workbench a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .workbench :is(a, button):focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 5px; }
  .workbench h1 { font-size: clamp(34px, 4vw, 49px); font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -1.9px; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 24px; }
  .intro-copy { color: var(--muted); font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 30px; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; align-items: center; }
  .primary-link, .build-prompt { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 14px; min-height: 48px; padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 8px; font: inherit; font-size: 15px; }
  .workbench .primary-link { color: var(--paper); background: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--ink); text-decoration: none; }
  .build-prompt { color: var(--muted); background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--line); cursor: pointer; }
  .build-prompt:hover { border-color: var(--muted); color: var(--ink); }
  .build-prompt:disabled { cursor: default; }
  .agent-marks { display: inline-flex; padding-left: 5px; }
  .agent-marks img { width: 24px; height: 24px; padding: 3px; border-radius: 50%; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--line); object-fit: contain; margin-left: -5px; }
  .copy-glyph { position: relative; width: 17px; height: 17px; }
  .copy-glyph svg { position: absolute; inset: 0; }
  .check-icon { opacity: 0; color: #397954; }
  [data-copied="true"] .copy-icon { opacity: 0; }
  [data-copied="true"] .check-icon { opacity: 1; }
  .copy-fallback { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.8; padding: 16px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; color: var(--muted); margin: 16px 0 0; }
  .copy-fallback span { display: block; user-select: all; }
  .intro-note { margin: 20px 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.8; }
  .intro-note a { text-decoration: underline; }
  .workbench section + section { margin-top: 54px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 40px; scroll-margin-top: 30px; }
  .workbench h2 { margin: 0 0 16px; font-size: 27px; letter-spacing: -.75px; font-weight: 620; line-height: 1.25; }
  .section-copy { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 26px; }
  .starter-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 9px; overflow: hidden; }
  .starter { padding: 24px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; text-decoration: none !important; }
  .starter + .starter { border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .starter:hover { background: var(--blume-muted, #fafafa); }
  .starter > svg { width: 23px; height: 23px; fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .starter > .ha-icon { color: #168db9; }
  .starter h3 { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 10px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .starter p { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .starter > span { margin-top: auto; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink); }
  .examples { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 28px; margin-top: 30px; }
  .example-label { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace), monospace; }
  .examples blockquote { margin: 18px 0 14px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; letter-spacing: -.35px; }
  .examples p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .examples a { font-size: 12px; }
  .example-note { font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--muted); margin: 28px 0 0; }
  .example-note a { text-decoration: underline; }
  .flow-diagram { display: flex; align-items: stretch; justify-content: space-between; gap: 9px; margin: 30px 0; }
  .flow-diagram > span { flex: 1; min-width: 0; padding: 17px 12px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 7px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 550; line-height: 1.5; }
  .flow-diagram .flow-hub { background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--ink); }
  .flow-diagram > b { align-self: center; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); }
  .flow-diagram small { display: block; font-size: 9px; line-height: 1.7; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 6px; opacity: .7; }
  .flow-notes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; }
  .flow-notes p { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }
  .flow-notes strong { font-weight: 550; color: var(--ink); }
  .interface-list { margin-top: 28px; }
  .interface-list a { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 82px 1fr 20px; gap: 20px; align-items: baseline; padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-decoration: none !important; }
  .interface-list a:hover p { color: var(--ink); }
  .interface-list span { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 550; }
  .interface-list p { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }
  .interface-list b { font-weight: 400; }
  .build-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr; gap: 44px; }
  .build-section .section-copy { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; }
  .build-section > div > p:not(.section-copy) { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }
  .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 18px; margin-top: 22px; font-size: 12px; }
  .closing p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 22px; }
  .closing > a:not(.primary-link) { display: inline-block; margin-left: 24px; font-size: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 1150px) { .starter { padding: 20px 16px; } .intro-copy { font-size: 17px; } .examples { gap: 22px; } .flow-diagram { gap: 6px; } }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .workbench { padding: 42px 24px; } .workbench h1 { font-size: 36px; letter-spacing: -1.2px; } }
  @media (max-width: 580px) {
    .desktop-break { display: none; } .workbench h1 { max-width: 9em; } .intro-copy { font-size: 16px; }
    .workbench section + section { margin-top: 36px; padding-top: 30px; } .workbench h2 { font-size: 25px; }
    .starter-grid, .examples, .flow-notes, .build-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .starter { padding: 22px; } .starter + .starter { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); } .starter > svg { margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .examples { gap: 28px; } .flow-notes { gap: 18px; } .build-section { gap: 22px; }
    .flow-diagram { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; } .flow-diagram > b { transform: rotate(90deg); } .flow-diagram small { font-size: 11px; }
    .interface-list a { grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr 14px; gap: 14px; }
  }
</style>
